Therefore, x'(s) is precisely the normalization of the original velocity vector, and so it is unit vector. 
Hence, the reparmetrized path x(s) has unit speed, regardless of the speed of the origiinal path x(t). 
(This result makes good geometric sense, too. 
If arclength, rather than time, is the parameter, then speed is measured in units of "length per length" which necessarily must be one)

